; rot: push 1 2 3, ROT rotates bottom element to top
; ROT semantics: a b c (c=top) → b c a (a=new top)
; Expected output: 1\n3\n2 (a=1 is new top, c=3 next, b=2 bottom)

PUSH 1         ; 0: push 1 (bottom)
PUSH 2         ; 1: push 2 (middle)
PUSH 3         ; 2: push 3 (top)
ROT            ; 3: stack becomes [2, 3, 1] (1 = new top)
OUTNUM         ; 4: print 1
OUTNUM         ; 5: print 3
OUTNUM         ; 6: print 2
HALT           ; 7
